{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["And he took butter and milk — by the plain sense of Scripture there was no need to state that he brought bread to the table; only the addition that he did not mention to them required saying that he brought. Bringing bread to the table is no novelty, but the butter and the meat, which is not ready for every guest, needed to be stated." "Standing over them — when one man is sitting and another is standing, he calls him 'standing over him.' And likewise: ״ואראה ה׳ יושב על כסאו״, seraphim standing above him. And likewise in Micaiah: ״וכל צבא השמים עומדים עליו מימינו ומשמאלו״." "Under the tree — the trees in the orchard."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:23.875993732Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}